## 2. `sendMessage` action (lines 332–363)

```typescript
sendMessage: (text) => {
    const { draftMedia, isStreaming } = get();
    const { currentModel } = useSettingsStore.getState();

    const readyMedia = draftMedia.filter((m) => m.dataUri).map((m) => m.dataUri!);
    const content = readyMedia.length > 0 ? Content.build(text, readyMedia) : text;

    if (Content.isEmpty(content)) {
      return;
    }

    // If streaming, enqueue instead of sending
    if (isStreaming) {
      get().enqueue(content, currentModel);
      set({ draftMedia: [] });
      return;                              // <-- returns without setting pendingInput
    }

    // Clear draft and set streaming state on active tab
    set(
      produce((draft: ChatState) => {
        clearAllInlineErrors(draft[draft.activeTab]);
        draft.draftMedia = [];
        draft[draft.activeTab].isStreaming = true;
        draft[draft.activeTab].pendingInput = { content, model: currentModel };  // <-- SETS pendingInput (line 356)
        syncFlatStateFromTab(draft, draft.activeTab);
        draft.handshakeReceived = false;
      }),
    );
    useApprovalStore.getState().clearRequests();

    doSend(get(), content, currentModel);
  },
```

**Key observations about `sendMessage`:**
- It **sets** `pendingInput` to `{ content, model: currentModel }` on line 356 when the message is actually sent.
- If the content is empty, it returns early without setting `pendingInput`.
- If already streaming, it enqueues the message and returns early **without** setting `pendingInput`.
- `sendMessage` itself **never clears** `pendingInput` to `null`.

